       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It adds no analgesic benefit beyond the ceiling.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). It would be better to use 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours as needed for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily.\n- **A different drug or dose**, if you were thinking of something else.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still advise against it."
      }
