       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum daily dose. There's no clinical indication I know of that justifies it. At that dose the risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm is high, and it adds no extra pain relief.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum dose)\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than these give, a multimodal approach would be safer, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen. A pharmacist or attending can help with that.\n\nIf you think an unusual dose is needed, please review it with your attending and the pharmacy first. They can enter it through a channel with the right safeguards. If you tell me which dose to use, I'll enter it now."
